## Why This Question Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to design a real-time monocular system integrating segmentation, 3D pose estimation with scene priors, grasp-point planning, and physics-based stability reasoning—plus efficient edge adaptation with minimal shots.

## Key Concepts

- Monocular 3D pose estimation using environmental priors
- Grasp-point prediction in cluttered scenes
- Differentiable physics modules for stability evaluation
- On-device few-shot adaptation strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode outline for the model heads
function forward(img, shelfPrior) {
  const features = backbone(img);
  const segmentation = segmentationHead(features);
  const pose = poseHead(features, shelfPrior);
  const grasp = graspHead(features, pose);
  const stability = physicsPrior(grasp, pose);
  return { segmentation, pose, grasp, stability };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design end-to-end computer vision systems that fuse perception with physics for deformable objects in cluttered environments, while also demonstrating expertise in efficient on-device adaptation.

## Key Concepts
- On-device few-shot adaptation
- 2.5D depth and surface normals representation
- Differentiable physics for stiffness estimation
- Grasp affordance learning with temporal consistency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: training loop for temporally-consistent affordance learning
for (batch of data) {
  const pred = model.forward(images);
  const affordanceLoss = computeBCE(pred.heatmap, target.heatmap);
  const depthLoss = computeL1(pred.depth, target.depth);
  const physicsLoss = computePhysicsConsistency(pred.stiffness, pred.depth);

  const totalLoss = affordanceLoss + depthLoss + physicsLoss;
  optimizer.step(totalLoss);
}

